From: PupJune2 <PupJune2@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 18:00:00 +0000
Subject: CromIKO settings

Add "CromIKO" at the top of Settings, with the mascot: all CromIKO
features in one place, instead of spread over Chromium's settings.

- A card with the mascot at the top, then four sections, each feature
  with its icon from the logo:
  - Protection: CromIKO DNS (with its status), the pop-up guard, ad
    blocking (Adblock Plus) and the weekly shield report (with the
    counts of the week).
  - Privacy: the incognito lock and when it locks (set right here, like
    in Privacy and security), the Fire button, and the incognito tab
    tile: a tap asks Android to add it to Quick Settings (Android 13 and
    newer; before, it says how).
  - Look and feel: the accent color, and Edit home screen, which opens
    its dialog. The new tab pages remember which widgets they have, so
    the dialog shows the same ones here.
  - Reading, videos and downloads: manga mode and the CromIKO player
    (where to find them), and the download manager.
- The settings stay where Chromium has them too.

The feature icons get their second color: the star of the logo in the
accent color, where nothing tints them, like in the settings. The menu,
the shortcuts and the buttons tint them in one color as before. New
icons for the mascot, the pop-up guard and the incognito tab tile.

The settings of Chromium 153 put every preference into a rounded
container and replace the background of its view. The tops of the
CromIKO pages (the CromIKO settings, the pop-up guard, the weekly shield
report and the download manager) now keep their tinted card, through
CromikoCardPreference.

